Everything in this repository is licensed under your choice of:

- the [Apache License 2.0](LICENSE-APACHE), or
- the [BSD-2-Clause Plus Patent License](LICENSE-BSD-2-CLAUSE-PATENT).

Both licenses carry a mandatory patent grant with defensive termination —
this disjunction is deliberate (unlike `MIT OR Apache-2.0`, there is no
election a licensee can make that avoids the patent grant). Apache-2.0 is
offered for corporate-legal familiarity; BSD-2-Clause-Patent for its
GPLv2 compatibility.

This is the *protocol tier* of the IdentiKey licensing doctrine: reference
implementations of specifications that are meant to outlive any single
steward. Embed them anywhere, commercially or otherwise — including in
products that compete with ours. That is the point.

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution intentionally
submitted for inclusion in this work by you shall be licensed as above,
without any additional terms or conditions (Apache-2.0 §5).
